      "group": "prober",
      "prediction": {
        "kind": "leaves",
        "band": {
          "low": 12,
          "high": 24.606
        },
        "text": "The algebra predicts a false removal: the replica can serve, but it leaves the EndpointSlice and the rules of each node. The band is 12 s to 24.606 s after the fault. The readiness check of the target fails for the hold (30 s), but its route still serves. Its latch trips 8 s–18 s after the fault. Then the controller of the service is not ready, thus the service refuses each request with a 503. The kubelet and the propagation (Cilium 1.20.4 sources: the reflector buffer (500 ms) and the BPF reconciler (1 ms), plus the shared path of CAL.T07.iptables (0.105 s)) remove the target 12 s–24.606 s after the fault: a false removal. Each connection to the target stays open, and the rules select a backend only for a new connection. Thus each request on those connections fails from the trip until the readiness of the service recovers, up to 6.16 s after the heal. 7–17 of the 24 connections are on the target, thus about 525–2992 requests fail."
      },
